From: User <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] aarch64: never issue clone3; threads and posix_spawn use clone

HAVE_CLONE3_WRAPPER is not defined for aarch64, so glibc takes its existing
"no clone3 wrapper" paths: __clone3_internal returns ENOSYS at once,
pthread_create and the other internal users issue clone, and posix_spawn
(and popen, system, pidfd_spawn) uses clone with the child resetting
signal dispositions itself; POSIX_SPAWN_SETCGROUP fails with ENOTSUP.

clone3 is not in the Android 13 and 14 app seccomp allowlist; the filter
traps it with SIGSYS, so glibc's retry with clone after ENOSYS never runs.
---
--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/aarch64/sysdep.h
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/aarch64/sysdep.h
@@ -179,7 +179,10 @@
 # define HAVE_GETTIMEOFDAY_VSYSCALL	"__kernel_gettimeofday"
 # define HAVE_GETRANDOM_VSYSCALL        "__kernel_getrandom"
 
-# define HAVE_CLONE3_WRAPPER		1
+/* HAVE_CLONE3_WRAPPER is deliberately not defined: the Android app seccomp
+   policy (API 33 and 34) traps clone3.  __clone3_internal then fails with
+   ENOSYS without a syscall, __clone_internal (pthread_create) and
+   __spawnix (posix_spawn) use clone directly.  */
 
 # undef INTERNAL_SYSCALL_RAW
 # define INTERNAL_SYSCALL_RAW(name, nr, args...)		\
